# 23. WHAT "LEARNING" MEANS IN AEGIS

The word "learning" must be controlled carefully.

It does not necessarily mean:

> "AI retrains itself automatically."

Instead, institutional learning may include:

- event summaries
- confirmed outcomes
- response effectiveness
- false-positive patterns
- false-negative investigations
- recurring environmental patterns
- workflow bottlenecks
- response delays
- resource constraints
- lessons learned
- policy updates
- protocol revisions
- baseline revisions
- preparedness recommendations

This makes the system resilient without pretending that every event should automatically modify an algorithm.

