# 26. PRODUCT ARCHITECTURE

AEGIS should be understood as a product ecosystem rather than one dashboard page.

The product has six conceptual capabilities.

## Capability A — Sensing

Answers:

> What is happening?

## Capability B — Intelligence

Answers:

> What could it mean?

## Capability C — Assessment

Answers:

> How significant is it?

## Capability D — Response

Answers:

> What should the organization do?

## Capability E — Verification

Answers:

> Did the response work?

## Capability F — Memory

Answers:

> What should the organization remember?

Therefore:

```text
AEGIS
│
├── SENSE
├── UNDERSTAND
├── ASSESS
├── RESPOND
├── VERIFY
└── REMEMBER
```

These six capabilities should drive product architecture.

They should not be interpreted as six invented screens.

