# 28. HUMAN-IN-THE-LOOP ARCHITECTURE

Human judgment is not an exception inside AEGIS.

It is part of the architecture.

```text
SYSTEM DETECTS
      ↓
SYSTEM EXPLAINS
      ↓
HUMAN REVIEWS
      ↓
HUMAN DECIDES
      ↓
SYSTEM RECORDS
      ↓
SYSTEM MONITORS
      ↓
HUMAN REVIEWS OUTCOME
```

This makes AEGIS accountable.

The interface must clearly distinguish:

- system-generated
- source-generated
- imported
- analyst-entered
- human-verified
- inferred
- uncertain
- historical
- simulated

No important piece of information should appear to have more authority than its provenance warrants.

