# 32. CONNECTIVITY STATE

Because resilience systems cannot assume perfect connectivity, AEGIS must explicitly represent:

```text
ONLINE
DEGRADED
DELAYED
PARTIAL DATA
OFFLINE
RECOVERING
```

A disconnected system should never display stale information as if it were live.

For example:

```text
LIVE
```

must mean something different from:

```text
LAST RECEIVED 17 MINUTES AGO
```

This is not cosmetic.

It is operational truth.

