# 72. NO SCREEN MAY INVENT ITS OWN TRUTH

If the same event appears in multiple screens:

```text
Screen A
Screen B
Screen C
```

they must reference the same underlying domain entity.

They must not each maintain independent versions.

Example:

If an event changes from:

```text
INVESTIGATING
```

to:

```text
ASSESSED
```

every relevant part of AEGIS should eventually reflect the same authoritative state.

This is the cure for cross-screen inconsistency.

